# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in what you need. Most of this file is optional.
#
# NO ELEVENLABS KEY. Nothing in this pipeline talks to ElevenLabs: every request is the
# site's, from the droplet, with a key belonging to the signed-in editor. The tools here
# report on lines, build the addon's data files and check them.

# Claude credentials for tools/rewrite-lore.mjs, which rewrites wiki articles into
# lore. Only that one command needs it -- scraping, the addon build and the voice
# pipeline all run without it. Responses are cached under tools/cache/rewrite/, so a
# re-run of an unchanged zone with an unchanged prompt costs nothing.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# CurseForge author token for scripts/release.sh, from
# https://authors-old.curseforge.com/account/api-tokens
#
# Tied to the account rather than to a project, so one token uploads all three.
# Only needed on the machine that publishes releases.
CURSEFORGE_TOKEN=

# The site's database -- one cluster for all three sections since the merge, on the
# default port. Unset, tools/voice/* fall back to reading tools/voice/manifest.json
# directly, which is all the addon build needs, so a clone with no Postgres can still
# package the addon.
#
# --dictionary-drift is the one selector that requires it: the dictionary a take would
# be compared against lives in the pronunciation_lexicon row, not in a file.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://localhost/spoken_quests_dev

# The site's accounts (BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, BETTER_AUTH_URL) and the master key its stored
# ElevenLabs credentials are sealed with (SPOKEN_SECRET_KEY) are not listed here, because
# `next dev` runs inside apps/web and would not read this file anyway. Locally all three
# have working defaults; in production all three are required and live in the droplet's
# shared/app.env -- see deploy/web/README.md.
#
# Registering grants no permissions, by design. Promote your local account by hand:
#   psql -d spoken_quests_dev \
#     -c "update \"user\" set role = 'admin' where email = 'you@example.com'"

# Nothing below is set locally, and setting any of it here would be a mistake.
#
# Every path under tools/ derives from ROOT in tools/lib/loredata.mjs, which is the
# module's own location -- correct for a script, and impossible once webpack has
# compiled it, because webpack replaces import.meta.url at build time. So the deployed
# site is told where its files are instead. These are the four, listed here so they are
# discoverable from the same place as everything else. They were ZONELORE_* until the two
# sites merged; the deployment they configure is /srv/spoken, and a variable naming
# the tree it no longer lives in is a variable somebody sets on the wrong box:
#
#   SPOKEN_ZONES_ROOT           the repo root: lore corpus, tools/voice/config*.json and pronunciation.json
#   SPOKEN_ZONES_SOUNDS         the audio store
#   SPOKEN_ZONES_AUDIO_HISTORY  superseded takes
#   SPOKEN_ZONES_MANIFEST       tools/voice/manifest.json
#
# Unset, each falls back to exactly the path it always had. The deployment's
# ecosystem.config.js is the only place they are set, and its README explains the split
# between the ones that live in a release and the ones that must not.
